  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BGD007N Bangladesh Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide vital relief to new refugee arrivals from Myanmar into Cox&apos;s Bazar, Bangladesh, a situation which is quickly degenrating into a humanitarian emergency with millions from a persecuted minority at risk of human trafficking, exploitation, and death from extreme conditions. The objective of the project is to reduce suffering and provide life-saving goods and services, specifically in the Shelter/NFI sector with a strong Protection component. The objective is to provide emergency shelter and basic NFI to vulnerable refugee households in makeshit, spontaneous, and informal settlements; activities are centered around distributions and training support, building on the observable preference of the population to make their own shelters rather than benefit from distributions/camp structures.</narrative>
  </description>
